{"results":[{"url":"https://wpde.com/news/local/sen-lindsay-graham-responds-to-president-trumps-coronavirus-response","final_url":"https://wpde.com/news/local/sen-lindsay-graham-responds-to-president-trumps-coronavirus-response","title":"Sen. Lindsey Graham responds to President Trump's Coronavirus response","description":"U. S. Senator Lindsey Graham (R-South Carolina) released a statement Wednesday evening on the announcement that President Trump has tapped Vice President Mike Pence to serve as coronavirus coordinator. His statement is below:&ldquo;I appreciate President Trump&rsquo;s determination and leadership and his administration&rsquo;s efforts to contain the spread of the coronavirus and keep our country safe.","language":"en","text":"# Sen. Lindsey Graham responds to President Trump's Coronavirus response\n\n---\n\nby Zuri Anderson\n\nWed, February 26, 2020 at 8:06 PM\n\nUpdated Wed, February 26, 2020 at 8:22 PM\n\nSenate Judiciary Committee Chairman Lindsey Graham, R-S.C., is surrounded by reporters after he and Republican lawmakers met with Attorney General William Barr about expiring provisions of the Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Act and other government intelligence laws, on Capitol Hill in Washington, Tuesday, Feb. 25, 2020. (J. Scott Applewhite/AP)\n\nWASHINGTON (WPDE) — U.S. Senator Lindsey Graham (R-South Carolina) released a statement Wednesday evening on the announcement that President Trump has tapped Vice President Mike Pence to serve as coronavirus coordinator.\n\nHis statement is below:\n\n> “I appreciate President Trump’s determination and leadership and his administration’s efforts to contain the spread of the coronavirus and keep our country safe.\n\n> “President Trump’s decision to put Vice President Pence in charge of our nation’s efforts to contain the coronavirus is an excellent idea and I have all the confidence in the world that the Vice President and his team will do everything in their power to contain this deadly virus.\n\n> “This is a difficult situation for the world at large. We must be agile and aggressive in our approach to containing this virus. I’m confident the Trump administration, working with Congress, will do everything possible to keep the American people safe and healthy.”","author":"Zuri Anderson","published_date":"2020-02-27T01:06:16.000Z","latency_ms":169.2033240001365,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}